{%- comment -%}
  Prepended to every layout, so the assigns below are in scope for
  full / half_horizontal / half_vertical / quadrant.

  Merge data comes from src/transform.js:
    fault       non-empty when the poll or the account is the problem
    sensors     every sensor, in the order Ruuvi returns them
    featured    the same sensors in the installer's priority order
    unmatched   priority entries that matched no sensor
    updated_at  "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM" in the viewer's zone
    stats       { total, alarms, low_battery, stale }

  Layouts read `featured`, never `sensors` — that is what makes the priority
  field steer the small screens. `sensors` stays available for a layout that
  wants Ruuvi's own order.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Custom fields (see settings.yml) are consumed in src/transform.js, not here:
    ruuvi_token          authenticates the poll, via polling_headers
    featured_sensors     orders `featured`, and fills `unmatched`
    stale_after_minutes  decides is_stale, and so status
  `trmnlp lint` only scans markup and the polling settings for field names, so
  without this note it reports the last two as unused.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
  /* Kept deliberately small: spacing, alignment, type, the grid and the corner
     radius are all framework classes in the markup. What is left here is only
     what the framework has no utility for — the card frame, the header rule,
     and making the card rows share the leftover height. */
  .ruuvi { gap: 0.75rem; block-size: 100%; }

  .ruuvi__header { border-block-end: 2px solid currentColor; }

  /* Equal rows, filling whatever height is left below the header. */
  .ruuvi__grid { grid-auto-rows: 1fr; flex: 1 1 auto; min-block-size: 0; }

  .ruuvi-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    border: 1.5px solid currentColor;
    min-inline-size: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  .ruuvi-card--primary { border-width: 3px; }
  /* A thick top edge marks a card that needs attention — legible from across
     the room, where a small chip is not. Replaces the Blade stylesheet's
     :has() rule; the condition is known in Liquid, so the class is just written. */
  .ruuvi-card--flagged { border-block-start-width: 8px; }

  .ruuvi-card__head { min-block-size: 1.25rem; }
  .ruuvi-card__name { line-height: 1.05; text-wrap: balance; }

  /* Icon, number and unit share a baseline; the row absorbs the slack so the
     stats and footer stay pinned to the bottom of the card. */
  .ruuvi-card__hero { align-items: baseline; flex: 1 1 auto; min-inline-size: 0; }

  .ruuvi-card__stats { border-block-start: 1.5px solid currentColor; }

  /* Right-aligned columns otherwise butt together, running the "hPa" and
     "Time" headers into one word. */
  .ruuvi-ledger th, .ruuvi-ledger td { padding-inline-start: 0.35rem; }

  /* data-clamp is driven by the framework's JS. Truncating in CSS as well
     keeps a long room name on one line even where that script has not run,
     and a wrapped name here costs the row below it. Capping the column also
     buys back the width that ran "hPa" and "Time" together in the header. */
  .ruuvi-ledger__name {
    display: block;
    max-inline-size: 14ch;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .ruuvi-icon { display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle; }
</style>

{%- assign primary = featured | first -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Staleness is drawn with the framework's gray text rather than opacity:
  opacity dithers badly on e-ink, and TRMNL's recipe review calls it out.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} Centred message, used for both the fault and empty states. {%- endcomment -%}
{% template notice %}
  <div class="layout layout--col layout--center">
    <span class="value value--small">{{ headline }}</span>
    <span class="label">{{ detail }}</span>
  </div>
{% endtemplate %}

{%- comment -%}
  Small chips for a sensor's exceptional states. {% render %} is scope
  isolated, so the sensor has to be passed in explicitly.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% template sensor_flags %}
  {%- if sensor.alarm %}<span class="label label--small label--outline">{{ sensor.alarm }}</span>{% endif -%}
  {%- if sensor.battery_low %}<span class="label label--small label--outline">bat</span>{% endif -%}
  {%- if sensor.is_stale %}<span class="label label--small label--gray 1bit:text--black">stale</span>{% endif -%}
{% endtemplate %}

{%- comment -%}
  One compact line: name on the left, readings on the right. Used by both
  half layouts, which differ only in how many lines fit and whether there is
  room for humidity.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% template sensor_line %}
  <div class="flex flex--row gap--small stretch-x{% if sensor.is_stale %} text--gray-30{% endif %}">
    <span class="label stretch-x" data-clamp="1">{{ sensor.name }}</span>
    {% render 'sensor_flags', sensor: sensor %}
    {%- if sensor.status == 'no_data' -%}
      <span class="value value--xsmall">&mdash;</span>
    {%- else -%}
      <span class="value value--small value--tnums">{{ sensor.temperature }}&deg;</span>
      {%- if with_humidity -%}
        <span class="value value--xsmall value--tnums">{{ sensor.humidity | default: '&mdash;' }}%</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{% endtemplate %}

{%- comment -%}
  Lucide icons (v1.16.0, ISC), inlined because a plugin cannot reference local
  assets. Sized by the caller; `currentColor` keeps them in step with the text
  around them, including the gray a stale card is drawn in.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% template icon %}
  {%- assign px = size | default: 24 -%}
  <svg class="ruuvi-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="{{ px }}" height="{{ px }}"
       viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
       stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
    {%- case name -%}
      {%- when 'thermometer' -%}
        <path d="M14 4v10.54a4 4 0 1 1-4 0V4a2 2 0 0 1 4 0Z" />
      {%- when 'thermometer-sun' -%}
        <path d="M12 2v2" /><path d="M12 8a4 4 0 0 0-1.645 7.647" /><path d="M2 12h2" />
        <path d="M20 14.54a4 4 0 1 1-4 0V4a2 2 0 0 1 4 0z" />
        <path d="m4.93 4.93 1.41 1.41" /><path d="m6.34 17.66-1.41 1.41" />
      {%- when 'thermometer-snowflake' -%}
        <path d="m10 20-1.25-2.5L6 18" /><path d="M10 4 8.75 6.5 6 6" /><path d="M10.585 15H10" />
        <path d="M2 12h6.5L10 9" /><path d="M20 14.54a4 4 0 1 1-4 0V4a2 2 0 0 1 4 0z" />
        <path d="m4 10 1.5 2L4 14" /><path d="m7 21 3-6-1.5-3" /><path d="m7 3 3 6h2" />
      {%- when 'battery-full' -%}
        <path d="M10 10v4" /><path d="M14 10v4" /><path d="M22 14v-4" /><path d="M6 10v4" />
        <rect x="2" y="6" width="16" height="12" rx="2" />
      {%- when 'battery-medium' -%}
        <path d="M10 14v-4" /><path d="M22 14v-4" /><path d="M6 14v-4" />
        <rect x="2" y="6" width="16" height="12" rx="2" />
      {%- when 'battery-low' -%}
        <path d="M22 14v-4" /><path d="M6 14v-4" />
        <rect x="2" y="6" width="16" height="12" rx="2" />
      {%- when 'battery' -%}
        <path d="M22 14v-4" /><rect x="2" y="6" width="16" height="12" rx="2" />
      {%- when 'droplet' -%}
        <path d="M12 22a7 7 0 0 0 7-7c0-2-1-3.9-3-5.5s-3.5-4-4-6.5c-.5 2.5-2 4.9-4 6.5C6 11.1 5 13 5 15a7 7 0 0 0 7 7z" />
      {%- when 'gauge' -%}
        <path d="m12 14 4-4" /><path d="M3.34 19a10 10 0 1 1 17.32 0" />
      {%- when 'clock' -%}
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" /><path d="M12 6v6l4 2" />
      {%- when 'triangle-alert' -%}
        <path d="m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3" />
        <path d="M12 9v4" /><path d="M12 17h.01" />
    {%- endcase -%}
  </svg>
{% endtemplate %}

{%- comment -%}
  One sensor as a card, for the large-screen grid in full.liquid.

  Sized for a ~240x190 box. That is what the device actually gives: it reports
  1872x1404, but renders at scale_factor 1.8, so the CSS canvas is ~1040x780
  and a 4-column grid leaves about 200px of content width per card.

  The flagged modifier replaces the stylesheet's `:has()` rule from the Blade
  original — the condition is known here, so the class can just be written.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% template sensor_card %}
  <article class="ruuvi-card py--3 px--4 rounded--small
      {%- if rank == 1 %} ruuvi-card--primary{% endif -%}
      {%- if sensor.alarm or sensor.battery_low %} ruuvi-card--flagged{% endif -%}
      {%- if sensor.is_stale %} text--gray-30{% endif -%}">
    {%- comment -%}
      The temperature icon rides in the head rather than beside the number,
      which the hero row needs the width for.

      Hero size is set by the widest reading, not by taste. value--tnums is
      tabular, so the minus and the decimal point are full digit widths:
      "-21.2" is five 0.6em glyphs, not three digits and two narrow marks.
      At value--large (58px) that is ~174px inside a ~204px card, and
      text_scale: large then overruns it — which is exactly what a freezer
      tag did on the device, twice. value--base (38px) needs ~114px and
      leaves room to spare.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="flex flex--row flex--center-y gap--xsmall ruuvi-card__head">
      <span class="label label--small label--gray 1bit:text--black">{{ rank_label }}</span>
      {% render 'icon', name: sensor.temp_icon, size: 16 %}
      <span class="stretch-x"></span>
      {%- if sensor.alarm -%}
        <span class="label label--small label--error">{% render 'icon', name: 'triangle-alert', size: 12 %} {{ sensor.alarm }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if sensor.is_stale -%}
        <span class="label label--small label--gray-out">{% render 'icon', name: 'clock', size: 12 %} stale</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {% render 'icon', name: sensor.battery_icon, size: 18 %}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      One line, clamped. "Living room freezer" is 19 characters and a real
      name; two lines here would cost the stats row its space.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <span class="title title--small ruuvi-card__name" data-clamp="1">{{ sensor.name }}</span>

    {%- comment -%}
      Icon sits beside the number rather than above it. Stacked, it cost 24px
      of height the card does not have.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if sensor.status == 'no_data' -%}
      <div class="flex flex--row flex--center-y gap--xsmall ruuvi-card__hero">
        <span class="value value--base">&mdash;</span>
      </div>
      <span class="label label--small label--gray 1bit:text--black">awaiting reading</span>
    {%- else -%}
      <div class="flex flex--row gap--xsmall ruuvi-card__hero">
        <span class="value value--base value--tnums">{{ sensor.temperature }}</span>
        <span class="value value--xsmall">&deg;C</span>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex--row flex--between flex--center-y pt--2 ruuvi-card__stats">
        <span class="value value--small value--tnums">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'droplet', size: 12 %} {{ sensor.humidity | default: '&mdash;' }}%
        </span>
        <span class="value value--small value--tnums">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'gauge', size: 12 %} {{ sensor.pressure_hpa | default: '&mdash;' }}
        </span>
      </div>

      <span class="label label--small label--gray 1bit:text--black">read {{ sensor.measured_at }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </article>
{% endtemplate %}
